# Settings for the relay. In development, copy this file to server/.env (git-ignored)
# and fill it in; the relay reads it at startup. In production, set these in the
# environment instead. See README.md for the other settings.

# SPORCLE_API_KEY (required)
#
# The Sporcle Party app's own API key. The relay sends it as the `x-sporcle-api-key`
# header on every call it makes to Sporcle (party.sporcle.com), next to the player's
# own id and token, the way the official app does. It identifies the app, not a
# person: every player's copy of Sporcle Party carries the same one. It belongs to
# Sporcle, so it isn't committed here.
#
# Where it comes from: Sporcle Party's Android app bundles its settings as text inside
# its JavaScript bundle, and the key is the `SPN_API_KEY=` line of the production
# settings (`ENV_NAME=prod`). To read it from an APK of the app:
#
#   unzip -p com.sporcle.party.apk assets/index.android.bundle > index.android.bundle
#   strings index.android.bundle | grep -o 'SPN_API_KEY=[0-9a-f]*' | sort -u
#
# The bundle is Hermes bytecode, but the settings are plain strings in it. The key
# changes only if Sporcle changes it in a new version of the app; the version the
# relay presents itself as is in lib/trivia_relay/sporcle/identity.ex.
SPORCLE_API_KEY=
